tables.doc:
ShellWrapTargetConfig is one shell-wrap target's recorded choice. The
native target's keys live directly in [shell_wrap] (ShellWrapConfig.Native);
the WSL bridge target's in [shell_wrap.windows].

SecurityKICSConfig is [security.scan.kics] (component
security.scan.kics). Its keys mean what [security.scan.trivy]'s do;
AllowRepoConfig covers the project's kics.config files.

leaves.doc:
ScheduleHours runs a full scan of each project active in the last
week once per this many hours. One of SecurityOpengrepScheduleHours;
0, the default, is off.

ReflogHoldMaxEntries caps how deep in a ref's reflog an entry still
holds a commit, the same way. One of SecurityReflogHoldMaxEntries;
0, the default, is none.

PentestPaceRPS is the most requests per second the run is asked to send;
the picker offers SecurityAssessmentsPaces, validation accepts 1 to 100.
A policy ceiling. Default 5.
